    <glyph id="PLASTOSEMIQUINONE" class="simple chemical" compartmentRef="thylakoid_membrane">
      <label text="Plastosemiquinone" />
      <bbox x="446.95" y="143.84" w="144.85" h="34.64" />
      <glyph id="PLASTOSEMIQUINONE__u0" class="unit of information">
        <label text="free radical" />
        <bbox x="452.95" y="134.84" w="84.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <extension>
        <qbo:annotation xmlns:qbo="https://dr-richard-barker.github.io/quantum-biology-atlas/qbo/1.0" entity="QBO:PLASTOSEMIQUINONE" evidenceTier="T3" confidence="inferred">
          <qbo:quantumClass>semiquinone_radical</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:quantumClass>radical_pair_donor</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:quantumClass>ros_leak_site</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:nucleus>1H</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:xref db="chebi">CHEBI:28377</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:rationale>The plastid counterpart of ubisemiquinone, and the same argument applies: a protein-bound organic radical with a measurable lifetime is the most credible site for field-dependent branching in the chain.
</qbo:rationale>
        </qbo:annotation>
      </extension>
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="CYTB6F_RIESKE" class="macromolecule" compartmentRef="thylakoid_membrane">
      <label text="Cyt b6f Rieske centre" />
      <bbox x="74.20" y="244.88" w="161.95" h="47.44" />
      <glyph id="CYTB6F_RIESKE__u0" class="unit of information">
        <label text="2Fe-2S" />
        <bbox x="80.20" y="235.88" w="42.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <glyph id="CYTB6F_RIESKE__u1" class="unit of information">
        <label text="Q cycle" />
        <bbox x="80.20" y="235.88" w="49.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <extension>
        <qbo:annotation xmlns:qbo="https://dr-richard-barker.github.io/quantum-biology-atlas/qbo/1.0" entity="QBO:CYTB6F_RIESKE" evidenceTier="T3" confidence="inferred">
          <qbo:quantumClass>rieske_2Fe2S</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:quantumClass>semiquinone_radical</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:nucleus>57Fe</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:nucleus>33S</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:nucleus>1H</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT4G03280</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="go_component">GO:0009512</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:rationale>Structurally and mechanistically the plastid twin of the mitochondrial Rieske centre (QBO:RIESKE_FES), with the same bifurcated Q-cycle chemistry. The review treats both as the same class of candidate target.
</qbo:rationale>
        </qbo:annotation>
      </extension>
    </glyph>
