    <glyph id="PSI_FES" class="complex" compartmentRef="thylakoid_membrane">
      <label text="Photosystem I Fe/S" />
      <bbox x="193.60" y="352.32" w="145.57" h="47.44" />
      <glyph id="PSI_FES__u0" class="unit of information">
        <label text="FX / FA / FB" />
        <bbox x="199.60" y="343.32" w="84.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <glyph id="PSI_FES__u1" class="unit of information">
        <label text="P700·+ A1·− pair" />
        <bbox x="199.60" y="343.32" w="112.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <extension>
        <qbo:annotation xmlns:qbo="https://dr-richard-barker.github.io/quantum-biology-atlas/qbo/1.0" entity="QBO:PSI_FES" evidenceTier="T2" confidence="reported">
          <qbo:quantumClass>iron_sulfur_4Fe4S</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:quantumClass>radical_pair_acceptor</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:quantumClass>triplet_yield_sensitive</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:nucleus>57Fe</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:nucleus>33S</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:nucleus>1H</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">ATCG01060</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="go_component">GO:0009522</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="ec">1.97.1.12</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:evidence ref="Parmagnani2023" doi="10.3390/ijms24032896" direction="altered" fieldRegime="NNMF">The geomagnetic field is required for normal lima bean photosynthesis, PSI/LHCI content and ROS production; near-null field conditions altered photosynthetic electron transport.
</qbo:evidence>
          <qbo:rationale>PSI is the strongest structural case in the whole atlas. Charge separation at P700 produces a genuine spin-correlated radical pair (P700·+ A1·−), which is the textbook example of the species the radical-pair mechanism describes — it is studied by exactly that formalism in photosynthesis spectroscopy. Three [4Fe-4S] clusters then carry the electron onward.
</qbo:rationale>
          <qbo:caveat>The P700·+ A1·− pair is extremely short-lived, and the well-characterised magnetic-field effects on it are seen in isolated preparations at fields far above geomagnetic. Structural plausibility is high; relevance at 50 uT is not established.
</qbo:caveat>
        </qbo:annotation>
      </extension>
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="THYLAKOID_ATP_SYNTHASE" class="complex" compartmentRef="thylakoid_membrane">
      <label text="ATP synthase" />
